-- statement:
--   The objects the formalized statements of *Coherence -generating power deviation: Fluctuations and input selectivity beyond average coherence generation* (arXiv:2609.19046) are stated in. Each was checked against the paper by a blind read-back and a moderator.
--
--   - `IsPopulation`: PDF p.2, (3): the entire closed probability simplex in reference-basis coordinates.
--   - `normalizePopulation`: PDF p.15, (E4): normalization of independent rate-one exponentials. The zero-sum input is a null event; its total-function value is the center.
--   - `simplexLaw`: PDF pp.2,15, (4),(E4): Dir(1,...,1), constructed without moment assumptions.
--   - `offDiagonal`: PDF p.2, (1): the complementary off-diagonal projection.
--   - `coherence`: PDF p.2, (2): squared Hilbert--Schmidt coherence, distinct from l1 coherence.
--   - `inputDensity`: PDF p.2, (3): the diagonal input with population p.
--   - `transition`: PDF p.3, (13): transition probabilities, computed from the matrix entries.
--   - `response`: PDF p.3, (14): the computed unitary coherence response.
--   - `zeroSumProjector`: PDF p.2, (7): projector onto all zero-sum population modes.
--   - `centered`: PDF p.2, (6): population displacement from the maximally mixed center.
--   - `quadratic`: PDF p.3, (15): a real quadratic form, including matrices not arising from dynamics.
--   - `generated`: PDF pp.2,9, (8),(75): actual coherence generated by a superoperator.
--   - `moment`: PDF pp.3,4, (9),(24),(25): actual kth moment under the simplex law.
--   - `cgp`: PDF p.3, (9): coherence-generating power is the first moment.
--   - `coherenceVariance`: PDF p.3, (9): actual central second moment.
--   - `cgpd`: PDF p.3, (9): nonnegative standard deviation.
--   - `coherenceLaw`: PDF p.3, (11): the full coherence-generation law.
--   - `partition`: PDF p.3, (10): moment generating function.
--   - `cumulant`: PDF p.3, (10): cumulant generating function.
--   - `fourthDenominator`: PDF p.4, (23): fourth-order Dirichlet denominator.
--   - `columnParticipation`: PDF p.4, (18): column inverse participation ratio.
--   - `rowParticipation`: PDF p.4, (30): row inverse participation ratio.
--   - `totalParticipation`: PDF p.4, (18): aggregate column participation.
--   - `realFrobeniusSq`: PDF p.4, (18): squared Frobenius norm on real population matrices.
--   - `diagonalSq`: PDF p.4, (19): squared Euclidean norm of the diagonal.
--   - `gammaFactor`: PDF p.5, before (35): dimensional fluctuation factor, used only for d>=2.
--   - `anisotropy`: PDF p.5, (35): the traceless anisotropic response; card>=2 in its results.
--   - `excess`: PDF p.5, (37): excess fluctuation, defined from the anisotropic response.
--   - `selectivity`: PDF p.6, (42): normalized selectivity, used only with positive mean and card>=2.
--   - `IsIncoherent`: PDF p.5: a monomial unitary permutes basis states and attaches unit-modulus phases.
--   - `IsFlat`: PDF p.6: a complex Hadamard unitary has flat transition probabilities.
--   - `generatedInBasis`: PDF p.5, (34): generated coherence in basis {V|i>}, expressed in ambient coordinates.
--   - `cgpInBasis`: PDF p.5, (34): mean in the rotated reference basis.
--   - `cgpdInBasis`: PDF p.5, (34): deviation in the rotated reference basis.
--   - `momentState`: PDF p.4, (20): integrated n-copy moment state; entrywise finite-dimensional integral.
--   - `risingDimension`: PDF p.4, (21): rising factorial, including its standard empty-product convention.
--   - `inverseWitness`: PDF p.5, (32): the explicit forward/inverse witness, with source row ordering.
--   - `blockPair`: PDF p.10, (82): two ordered 2-by-2 blocks on Fin 4, first block first.
--   - `localized`: PDF p.10, (82): localized two-level response embedded in dimension four.
--   - `distributed`: PDF p.10, (82): distributed pair of two-level responses.
--   - `uniformProjector`: PDF p.14, (D1): uniform population projector.
--   - `completeAdjacency`: PDF p.10, (87): complete graph adjacency in vertex coordinates.
--   - `starAdjacency`: PDF p.10, (87): star adjacency, with vertex 0 the hub.
--   - `walk`: PDF p.10, (87): spectral normalization, using the frozen operator norm.
--   - `leafProjector`: PDF p.14, (D5): zero hub block plus the leaf zero-sum projector.
--   - `leafState`: PDF p.14, (D3): normalized uniform leaf state (used with d>=2).
--   - `empiricalMean`: PDF p.8, (62): exactly observed empirical coherence mean.
--   - `sampleVariance`: PDF p.8, (65): unbiased sample variance; results use N>=2.
--   - `fourthCentral`: PDF p.8, (66): fourth central moment.
--   - `sampleLaw`: PDF p.8, (66): canonical independent N-sample law.
--   - `LawsConverge`: PDF p.8, (66): weak convergence of laws, tested on bounded continuous real functions. This permits varying finite sample spaces and a zero-variance Dirac Gaussian.
--   - `tiltedLaw`: PDF p.8, (67): normalized exponential tilt, not an unnormalized weighted average.
--   - `tiltedMean`: PDF p.8, (68): mean under the normalized tilted probability law.
--   - `coherenceObservable`: PDF p.8, (70): swap minus its dephasing, on two ordered copies.
--   - `fourCopyObservable`: PDF p.8, (72): K on copies (0,1) times K on copies (2,3).
--   - `channelOutput`: PDF p.9, (73): coherent output from the ith basis projector.
